module slice_vs_range.neg_2

// A RANGE USED AS A VALUE, `ro r = 1..3` -- and the refusal must keep naming
// the head of a `for`, because here that is the true thing to say.
//
// THE CONTROL HALF of registry 1170, and it is the half that makes the pair a
// measurement. Splitting one text into two is easy to do wrongly in the other
// direction: give every `..` the slice wording and the slice fixture goes
// green while this line starts lying instead. A distinction is only shown by
// two cells that must hold DIFFERENT texts at the same time.
//
// This form is legal Nova -- the oracle accepts it -- and it is the subset
// that does not compile it yet (F35). That is why the refusal says "not a
// value" rather than claiming the language forbids it.

// NOVAC_EXPECT a range is a `for` head here, not a value

fn f() -> () {
    ro r = 1..3
}
